{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And he looked, and behold a well in the field, and behold, there were three flocks of sheep lying by it</b> Scripture elaborates in this narrative to inform us that those who hope in YHWH will renew their strength, and His fear gives might. For behold, Jacob our father came from the road and he was weary, yet he alone rolled away the stone that all the shepherds and the three flocks of sheep — which had many shepherds and guards, all of them lying by it — were not able to move at all. And to our Rabbis in Bereshit Rabbah (Genesis Rabbah 70:8), this too holds for them a hidden allusion to the future: for it so befell him that he entered by way of the well, and not all the flocks were gathered but only three of them, and he came at the time when the stone was over the mouth of the well and the flocks were guarding it. And the entire matter recounted here was to inform him that he would succeed on this path, and from him would come forth seed worthy of this allusion. For the well alludes to the Temple, and the three flocks of sheep are those who go up on the three festivals, \"for from that well they would water the flocks\" — for from there they would draw the Holy Spirit. Or it may allude to \"for out of Zion shall go forth Torah\" (Isaiah 2:3), which is likened to water (Bava Kamma 17a), \"and the word of YHWH from Jerusalem.\" \"And there all the flocks were gathered\" — coming from the entrance of Hamath to the brook of Egypt (I Kings 8:65); \"and they rolled the stone and watered\" — for from there they would draw the Holy Spirit; \"and they returned the stone\" — set back in its customary place:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {0 "The abbreviation 'ב\"ק' is resolved as Bava Kamma, following the standard Talmudic reference to Torah being likened to water, which appears in Bava Kamma 17a (and parallel passages). The phrase מֻנָּח לָרֶגֶל הַבָּא appears to conclude the comment by noting the stone was returned to its routine position."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:36:32.691421035Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}